#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:2
msgid "Attribute-Based Access Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/_static/badges/entry-adv.rst:7
msgid ""
"|plans-img-yellow| Available on `Entry and Enterprise Advanced "
"<https://mattermost.com/pricing/>`__ plans"
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:6
msgid "plans-img-yellow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:16
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v10.9, system admins in large or complex organizations "
"who require Zero Trust Security when handling with sensitive information "
"can prevent unauthorized access through attribute-based access controls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:18
msgid ""
"Enforcing strict access controls based on user attributes eliminates "
"manual role adjustment processes that can lead to security risks, "
"inefficiencies, or inappropriate access, while maintaining security and "
"compliance by ensuring that only authorized users can access specific "
"Mattermost channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:20
msgid ""
"Attribute-based access control (ABAC) can be used with the following "
"policy types:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:22
msgid ""
"**System-wide access policies** (managed by System Admins): Centralized "
"policies created in the System Console that can be applied across "
"multiple channels. See :doc:`System-wide attribute-based access policies "
"</administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-system-wide-policies>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:23
msgid ""
"**Permission policies** (managed by System Admins): Attribute-based "
"restrictions on user actions such as file upload and file download. See "
":ref:`Permission policies <administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-system-"
"wide-policies:permission policies>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:24
msgid ""
"**Team-scoped membership policies** (managed by Team Admins): Channel "
"membership policies that Team Admins can create, edit, and delete "
"directly from Team Settings for channels in their team. See :ref:`Manage "
"team-scoped membership policies in Team Settings <administration-"
"guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules:manage team-scoped "
"membership policies in team settings>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:25
msgid ""
"**Channel-specific access rules** (managed by Channel Admins): Self-"
"service access rules that Channel Admins can configure directly in "
"Channel Settings for individual channels. See :doc:`Channel-specific "
"access rules </administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-"
"rules>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:28
msgid "Before you begin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:30
msgid ""
"Attribute-based access controls require defined user attributes that are "
"either synchronized from an external system (such as LDAP or SAML) or "
"manually configured and enabled on your Mattermost server. You'll need to"
" :doc:`configure user attributes </administration-guide/manage/admin"
"/user-attributes>` in the System Console first before creating access "
"policies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:32
msgid ""
"Each attribute becomes a user profile option users can populate, unless "
"you disable the **Editable by Users** option, available from Mattermost "
"v11. Admin-managed attributes can be used in addition to the LDAP/SAML "
"synchronized attributes for attribute-based access control rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:34
msgid ""
"Once user attributes are defined, go to **System Console > System "
"Attributes > Attribute-Based Access** to enable attribute-based access "
"controls for your Mattermost instance. This functionality requires a "
"Mattermost Enterprise Advanced license."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:36
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v10.11, user-managed attributes are excluded from "
"attribute-based access control (ABAC) rules by default for security "
"reasons. This prevents access control policies from being circumvented by"
" users editing their own profile attributes. To include user-managed "
"attributes in ABAC rules, a system admin must explicitly enable the "
"``EnableUserManagedAttributes`` configuration setting. See the :ref:`user"
" attribute <administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes:before you "
"begin>` documentation for details on enabling this feature. This "
"configuration setting is available only in Enterprise Edition Advanced "
"and is disabled by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:39
msgid "Configure access policies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:41
msgid ""
"Once enabled, you have multiple ways to configure access policies in "
"Mattermost:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:43
msgid "**System Admins can:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:45
msgid ""
"Create :doc:`system-wide access policies </administration-"
"guide/manage/admin/abac-system-wide-policies>` that can be assigned "
"across multiple channels in the System Console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:46
msgid ""
"Assign :ref:`individual channel policies <administration-"
"guide/manage/admin/abac-system-wide-policies:define access controls per "
"channel>` to specific channels in the System Console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:47
msgid ""
"Define :ref:`permission policies <administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-"
"system-wide-policies:permission policies>` that restrict actions such as "
"file upload and file download based on user attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:49
#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:53
msgid "**Team Admins can:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:51
msgid ""
"Create, edit, and delete :ref:`team-scoped channel membership policies "
"<administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules:manage team-"
"scoped membership policies in team settings>` for channels in their team "
"directly from Team Settings, when granted the "
"``manage_team_access_rules`` permission."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:55
msgid ""
"Create and manage :doc:`team-level channel membership policies "
"</administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-team-channel-policies>` in Team "
"Settings, scoping attribute-based rules to one or more private channels "
"within their team."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:57
msgid "**Channel Admins can:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control.rst:59
msgid ""
"Configure :doc:`channel-specific access rules </administration-"
"guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules>` directly in Channel "
"Settings without requiring a system admin."
msgstr ""

